{% block title %}Notices{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<h1>Notices</h1>
<p>The code of this service and its scan rules are MIT licensed. Their source and the build files of every image are at <a href="https://github.com/infinito-nexus/quality">github.com/infinito-nexus/quality</a>, where <code>flake.nix</code> names the packages below and <code>flake.lock</code> pins their revisions.</p>
<h2>Scan and proxy images</h2>
<p>The scan image bundles every package below except squid, which the proxy image bundles, each with its runtime dependencies. All of them are built from nixpkgs revision <code>1d060086d60cb76a40cf37109f979d88a5bd6396</code> (nixos-unstable), except semgrep, which is built from nixpkgs revision <code>c56a87d8e41ce69bd2af57eb35dcc117a9dfca33</code> (nixos-26.05), and jscpd, which <code>flake.nix</code> takes from its prebuilt release on npm because nixpkgs has no jscpd, one per platform, which <code>flake.lock</code> pins as the inputs <code>jscpd-x86_64-linux</code> and <code>jscpd-aarch64-linux</code>. <code>flake.nix</code> also takes import-linter from its wheel on PyPI, its graph library grimp (BSD-2-Clause, <a href="https://github.com/python-grimp/grimp">github.com/python-grimp/grimp</a>) from its prebuilt wheel on PyPI, one per platform, and dependency-cruiser from its release tag on GitHub, because nixpkgs has none of them, which <code>flake.lock</code> pins as the inputs <code>import-linter</code>, <code>grimp-x86_64-linux</code>, <code>grimp-aarch64-linux</code> and <code>dependency-cruiser</code>. Each licence is the one nixpkgs declares for the package at that revision, and for jscpd, import-linter, grimp and dependency-cruiser the one <code>flake.nix</code> declares.</p>
