<h2>Source code</h2>
<p>nixpkgs at <a href="https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs">github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs</a> holds, at the revisions above, the build recipe and the patches of every package and pins its upstream source by hash. <code>nix build github:NixOS/nixpkgs/&lt;revision&gt;#&lt;attribute&gt;.src</code> fetches that upstream source, for example for the GPL licensed bash, coreutils, git, hadolint, shellcheck and squid.</p>
<h2>Web image</h2>
<p>The web image builds on the official Docker image <code>python:3.14-slim-trixie</code>. Its Debian packages carry their own licences, and their source is in the Debian archive at <a href="https://sources.debian.org">sources.debian.org</a>. On top of it, the image adds these Python packages from PyPI, pinned in <code>service/web/requirements.txt</code>, and the ALTCHA widget from npm. Each licence is the one the package metadata declares.</p>
